    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30949" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nī^gris</span></b> , is (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nī^gir</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8, 2,
		6</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nī^-ger</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 6, § 673</span></i>),
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in the interior of Africa</i>, now <i>the
				Joliba</i> or <i>Niger</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 4,
				4, § 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 21, 32, § 77</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nī^grītae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the people living near the Niger</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 4,
			3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 10, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 8, 8, § 43</span></i>.</div>
